{# req026 — gateway-wide cap on request body size.

   Two patches in one EnvoyFilter:

   1. HTTP_FILTER inserts `envoy.filters.http.buffer` BEFORE the
      router on every GATEWAY listener with `max_request_bytes` =
      apps_streaming_max_request_bytes. Any inbound request whose
      body exceeds the cap is rejected with HTTP 413 + "Payload Too
      Large" (text/plain) BEFORE the bytes reach the backend.

   2. HTTP_ROUTE per-route DISABLES the buffer filter for the
      WebSocket upgrade route (`/ws`). Without this, the buffer
      filter waits for the full request body before calling the
      router; a WS upgrade has no body and never closes the request,
      so the handshake hangs until client timeout (verified in
      production: response_flags=DC, upstream_host=null, no upstream
      log of the request). Route name follows Istio's deterministic
      `<namespace>.<httproute>.<ruleIndex>` convention — keep
      `apps_streaming_websocket_route_name` in sync when the
      HTTPRoute rule order changes.

   Why gateway-wide and not per-route enable:
   - The clean per-route override (`BufferPerRoute` enable via
     `applyTo: HTTP_ROUTE` MERGE with route.action: ANY) overwrites
     every route's `match` block in Istio 1.26 (RHCL 1.3.4 and 1.4.x alike) and
     breaks all routing. The route-name match works for DISABLE
     (this patch) but is too brittle for ENABLE because we'd have
     to track the upload rule's index across template edits.
   - A gateway-wide cap is what most production setups actually do:
     "no inbound request may exceed N MiB, period."

   Side effects on other endpoints:
   - WebSocket upgrades (/ws): explicitly disabled (patch 2). Required.
   - SSE / AI streaming response: response streaming, not request
     body — buffer filter only touches REQUEST, so unaffected.
   - AI prompt POSTs, transfers, applications: typical bodies <100 KiB,
     well below the 32 MiB cap.

   AuthPolicy interaction: Authorino's ext_authz filter sits before
   the router and (with the default `with_request_body: false`) reads
   only headers — auth still runs first, body cap second. An
   unauthenticated 100 MiB upload gets a 401 from Authorino without
   ever buffering. Do NOT flip `with_request_body` on any AuthConfig
   that fronts this gateway, or the rejection order changes.

   The complementary upload TIMEOUT is set on the HTTPRoute itself
   via `spec.rules[].timeouts.request` — see connectivity-httproute.yml.j2.
#}
apiVersion: networking.istio.io/v1alpha3
kind: EnvoyFilter
metadata:
  name: {{ apps_streaming_envoyfilter_name }}
  namespace: {{ apps_streaming_envoyfilter_namespace }}
  labels:
    app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: ansible
    app.kubernetes.io/part-of: rhcl-apps
    rhcl.poc/req: req026
spec:
  workloadSelector:
    labels:
      gateway.networking.k8s.io/gateway-name: {{ apps_connectivity_gateway_name }}
  configPatches:
    - applyTo: HTTP_FILTER
      match:
        context: GATEWAY
        listener:
          filterChain:
            filter:
              name: envoy.filters.network.http_connection_manager
              subFilter:
                name: envoy.filters.http.router
      patch:
        operation: INSERT_BEFORE
        value:
          name: envoy.filters.http.buffer
          typed_config:
            "@type": type.googleapis.com/envoy.extensions.filters.http.buffer.v3.Buffer
            max_request_bytes: {{ apps_streaming_max_request_bytes }}
    - applyTo: HTTP_ROUTE
      match:
        context: GATEWAY
        routeConfiguration:
          vhost:
            route:
              name: {{ apps_streaming_websocket_route_name | string | to_json }}
      patch:
        operation: MERGE
        value:
          typed_per_filter_config:
            envoy.filters.http.buffer:
              "@type": type.googleapis.com/envoy.extensions.filters.http.buffer.v3.BufferPerRoute
              disabled: true
